@lang en
IMPORT `msig-cgl-part-cgl`

-- PRODUCTS AND COMPLETED OPERATIONS LIABILITY INSURANCE COVERAGE PART (src:557-692).
-- Same shape as the CGL part, with three differences that matter: the insuring agreement
-- reaches only harm within the completed operations hazard or the products hazard; the
-- exclusions are nine, (a)-(i), and exclusion (a) has no incidental-contract exception;
-- Persons Insured has no paragraph (e). The CGL part is imported only for Persons Insured
-- (a)-(c), whose wording is the same in both parts, and for the arithmetic of the cap in
-- III; each use says so.
--
-- Special Conditions that reach only this part (the Business Risk Exclusion, the Claims
-- Made Basis Endorsement, the Claim Series Clause) are in msig-cgl-special.l4.

§ `PRODUCTS AND COMPLETED OPERATIONS LIABILITY INSURANCE COVERAGE PART`
-- src:557 | PRODUCTS AND COMPLETED OPERATIONS LIABILITY INSURANCE COVERAGE PART

§§ `I. COVERAGE A – BODILY INJURY LIABILITY; COVERAGE B – PROPERTY DAMAGE LIABILITY`

-- src:559 | l. COVERAGE A – BODILY INJURY LIABILITY
-- src:561 | COVERAGE B – PROPERTY DAMAGE LIABILITY
-- src:563 | The Company will pay on behalf of the insured all sums which the insured shall become legally obligated to pay as damages
-- src:564 | because of
-- src:566 | A. bodily injury or
-- src:568 | B. property damage
-- src:570 | to which this insurance applies, caused by an occurrence, if the bodily injury or property damage is included within the
-- src:571 | completed operations hazard or the products hazard, and the Company shall have the right and duty to defend any suit
-- src:572 | against the insured seeking damages on account of such bodily injury or property damage, even if any allegations of the suit
-- src:573 | are groundless, false or fraudulent, and make such investigation and settlement of any claim or suit as it deems expedient,
-- src:574 | but the Company shall not be obligated to pay any claim or judgement or to defend any suit after the applicable limit of the
-- src:575 | Company's liability has been exhausted by payment of judgements or settlements.
@ref src:563-570
GIVEN policy     IS A `The policy as declared`
      claim      IS A `A claim against an insured`
      d          IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`P&CO I — the insuring agreement reaches the claim` policy claim d MEANS
        `for` claim `,` `the insured is legally obligated to pay the sums claimed as damages`
    AND `the harm is bodily injury or property damage as defined` policy claim d
    AND `the harm was caused by an occurrence` claim

@ref src:570
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`P&CO I — the harm is within the completed operations hazard or the products hazard` claim MEANS
        `the harm is included within the completed operations hazard` claim
    OR  `the harm is included within the products hazard` claim

§§ `Exclusions`
-- src:577 | Exclusions
-- src:579 | This insurance does not apply:

-- Unlike CGL exclusion (a), there is no "except an incidental contract".
-- src:581 | (a) to liability assumed by the insured under any contract or agreement; but this exclusion does not apply to a warranty of
-- src:582 | fitness or quality of the named insured's products or a warranty that work performed by or on behalf of the named
-- src:583 | insured will be done in a workmanlike manner;
@ref src:581-583
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`P&CO exclusion (a) applies` claim MEANS
        `for` claim `,` `the insured assumed liability for the harm under a contract or agreement`
    AND NOT "but" ... (    `for` claim `,` `the liability is under a warranty of fitness or quality of the named insured's products`
                       OR  `for` claim `,` `the liability is under a warranty that work performed by or on behalf of the named insured will be done in a workmanlike manner`)

-- As CGL (h), but of "the insured" alone: no "or his indemnitee".
-- src:585 | (b) to bodily injury or property damage for which the insured may be held liable
-- src:587 | (1) as a person or organization engaged in the business of manufacturing, distributing, selling or serving alcoholic
-- src:588 | beverages, or
-- src:590 | (2) if not so engaged, as an owner or lessor of premises used for such purposes,
-- src:592 | if such liability is imposed
-- src:594 | (i) by, or because of the violation of, any statute, ordinance or regulation pertaining to the sale, gift, distribution or use
-- src:595 | of any alcoholic beverage, or
-- src:597 | (ii) by reason of the selling, serving or giving of any alcoholic beverage to a minor or to a person under the influence of
-- src:598 | alcohol or which causes or contributes to the intoxication of any person;
-- src:600 | but part (ii) of this exclusion does not apply with respect to liability of the insured as an owner or lessor described in (2)
-- src:601 | above;
@ref src:585-601
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`P&CO exclusion (b) applies` claim MEANS
        "(1)" ... `for` claim `,` `the insured may be held liable as a person or organization engaged in the business of manufacturing, distributing, selling or serving alcoholic beverages`
              AND (    "(i)" ... `for` claim `,` `the liability is imposed by, or because of the violation of, a statute, ordinance or regulation pertaining to the sale, gift, distribution or use of an alcoholic beverage`
                   OR "(ii)" ... `for` claim `,` `the liability is imposed by reason of selling, serving or giving an alcoholic beverage to a minor or to a person under the influence of alcohol, or which causes or contributes to the intoxication of a person`)
    OR  "(2)" ... `for` claim `,` `the insured may be held liable, not being so engaged, as an owner or lessor of premises used for such purposes`
              AND "(i)" ... `for` claim `,` `the liability is imposed by, or because of the violation of, a statute, ordinance or regulation pertaining to the sale, gift, distribution or use of an alcoholic beverage`

-- src:603 | (c) to any obligation for which the insured or any carrier as his insurer may be held liable under any workmen's
-- src:604 | compensation, unemployment compensation or disability benefits law, or under any similar law;
@ref src:603-604
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`P&CO exclusion (c) applies` claim MEANS
    `for` claim `,` `the claim is for an obligation for which the insured or a carrier as its insurer may be held liable under a workmen's compensation, unemployment compensation or disability benefits law, or a similar law`

-- Unlike CGL (j), no exception for liability assumed under an incidental contract.
-- src:606 | (d) to bodily injury to any employee of the insured arising out of and in the course of his employment by the insured or to
-- src:607 | any obligation of the insured to indemnify another because of damages arising out of such injury;
@ref src:606-607
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`P&CO exclusion (d) applies` claim MEANS
        `the harm is bodily injury` claim
    AND `for` claim `,` `the bodily injury is to an employee of the insured, arising out of and in the course of employment by the insured`

-- src:609 | (e) to loss of use of tangible property which has not been physically injured or destroyed resulting from
-- src:611 | (1) a delay in or lack of performance by or on behalf of the named insured of any contract or agreement, or
-- src:613 | (2) the failure of the named insured's products or work performed by or on behalf of the named insured to meet the
-- src:614 | level of performance, quality, fitness or durability warranted or represented by the named insured;
-- src:616 | but this exclusion does not apply to loss of use of other tangible property resulting from the sudden and accidental
-- src:617 | physical injury to or destruction of the named insured products or work performed by or on the named insured after such
-- src:618 | products or work have been put to use by any person or organization other than an insured;
@ref src:609-618
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`P&CO exclusion (e) applies` claim MEANS
        claim's `the harm` EQUALS `loss of use of tangible property which has not been physically injured or destroyed`
    AND (   "(1)" ... `for` claim `,` `the loss of use results from a delay in or lack of performance by or on behalf of the named insured of a contract or agreement`
         OR "(2)" ... `for` claim `,` `the loss of use results from the failure of the named insured's products or work performed by or on behalf of the named insured to meet the level of performance, quality, fitness or durability warranted or represented by the named insured`)
    AND NOT "but" ... `for` claim `,` `the loss of use results from sudden and accidental physical injury to or destruction of the named insured's products or work performed by or on behalf of the named insured, after they had been put to use by a person or organization other than an insured`

-- src:620 | (f) to property damage to the named insured's products arising out of such products or any part of such products;
@ref src:620
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`P&CO exclusion (f) applies` claim MEANS
        `the harm is property damage` claim
    AND `for` claim `,` `the damaged property is the named insured's products`
    AND `for` claim `,` `the property damage arises out of those products or any part of them`

-- src:622 | (g) to property damage to work performed by or on behalf of the named insured arising out of the work or any portion
-- src:623 | thereof, or out of materials, parts or equipment furnished in connection therewith;
@ref src:622-623
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`P&CO exclusion (g) applies` claim MEANS
        `the harm is property damage` claim
    AND `for` claim `,` `the damaged property is work performed by or on behalf of the named insured`
    AND `for` claim `,` `the property damage arises out of that work or any portion of it, or out of materials, parts or equipment furnished in connection with it`

-- src:625 | (h) to damages claimed for the withdrawal, inspection, repair, replacement, or loss of use of the named insured's products
-- src:626 | or work completed by or for the named insured or of any property of which such products or work form a part, if such
-- src:627 | products, work or property are withdrawn from the market or from use because of any known or suspected defect or
-- src:628 | deficiency therein;
@ref src:625-628
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`P&CO exclusion (h) applies` claim MEANS
        `for` claim `,` `the damages are claimed for the withdrawal, inspection, repair, replacement or loss of use of the named insured's products or work completed by or for the named insured, or of property of which they form a part`
    AND `for` claim `,` `those products, that work or that property were withdrawn from the market or from use because of a known or suspected defect or deficiency in them`

-- src:630 | (i) to bodily injury or property damage arising out of discharge, dispersal, release or escape of smoke, vapors, soot, fumes,
-- src:635 | acids, alkalis, toxic chemicals, liquids or gases, waste materials or other irritants, contaminants or pollutants into or
-- src:636 | upon land, the atmosphere or any water course or body of water; but this exclusion does not apply if such discharge,
-- src:637 | dispersal, release or escape is sudden and accidental.
@ref src:630-637
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`P&CO exclusion (i) applies` claim MEANS
        `for` claim `,` `the harm arises out of the discharge, dispersal, release or escape of smoke, vapors, soot, fumes, acids, alkalis, toxic chemicals, liquids or gases, waste materials or other irritants, contaminants or pollutants into or upon land, the atmosphere or a water course or body of water`
    AND NOT "but" ... `for` claim `,` `that discharge, dispersal, release or escape was sudden and accidental`

§§ `II. PERSONS INSURED`

-- (a)-(c) are word for word those of the CGL part (src:464-473), so the CGL rule is used;
-- (d) is the same real estate manager; there is no (e).
-- src:641 | II. PERSONS INSURED
-- src:643 | Each of the following is an insured under this insurance to the extent set forth below:
-- src:645 | (a) if the named insured is designated in the declarations as an individual, the person so designated but only with respect to
-- src:646 | the conduct of a business of which he is the sole proprietor, and the spouse of the named insured with respect to the
-- src:647 | conduct of such a business;
-- src:649 | (b) if the named insured is designated in the declarations as a partnership or joint venture, the partnership or joint venture so
-- src:650 | designated and any partner or member thereof but only with respect to his liability as such;
-- src:652 | (c) if the named insured is designated in the declarations as other than an individual, partnership or joint venture, the
-- src:653 | organization so designated and any executive officer, director or stockholder thereof while acting within the scope of his
-- src:654 | duties as such;
-- src:656 | (d) any person (other than an employee of the named insured ) or organization while acting as real estate manager for the
-- src:657 | named insured.
@ref src:641-657, 281-285
GIVEN policy IS A `The policy as declared`
      claim  IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`P&CO II — the person claimed against is an insured` policy claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `the person claimed against`
    WHEN `a person who is not an employee of the named insured, or an organization, acting as real estate manager for the named insured` THEN
        "(d)" ... TRUE
    WHEN `the legal representative of the named insured, who has died` THEN
        `Condition 8 — on the named insured's death, the person claimed against is an insured` claim
    WHEN `the person having proper temporary custody of the property of the named insured, who has died` THEN
        `Condition 8 — on the named insured's death, the person claimed against is an insured` claim
    OTHERWISE `Persons Insured (a)-(c) — the named insured or a person of it is an insured` policy claim

-- src:659 | This insurance does not apply to bodily injury or property damage arising out of the conduct of any partnership or joint
-- src:660 | venture of which the insured is a partner or member and which is not designated in this Policy as a named insured.
@ref src:659-660
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`P&CO II — the undesignated partnership or joint venture exclusion applies` claim MEANS
    `for` claim `,` `the harm arises out of the conduct of a partnership or joint venture of which the insured is a partner or member and which is not designated in the Policy as a named insured`

§§ `III. LIMITS OF LIABILITY`

-- As printed: each aggregate reaches ALL bodily injury, or ALL property damage, "to which
-- this coverage applies". The cap arithmetic is the CGL part's `the cap of`.
-- src:663 | III. LIMITS OF LIABILITY
-- src:665 | Regardless of the number of (1) insureds under this Policy, (2) persons or organizations who sustain bodily injury or property
-- src:666 | damage, or (3) claims made or suit brought on account of bodily injury or property damage, the Company's liability is limited
-- src:667 | as follows:
-- src:669 | Coverage A - The total liability of the Company for all damages, including damages for care and loss of services, because of
-- src:670 | bodily injury sustained by one or more persons as the result of any one occurrence shall not exceed the limit of bodily injury
-- src:671 | liability stated in the schedule as applicable to "each occurrence".
-- src:673 | Subject to the above provision respecting "each occurrence", the total liability of the Company for all damages because of
-- src:674 | all bodily injury to which this coverage applies shall not exceed the limit of bodily injury liability stated in the schedule as
-- src:675 | "aggregate".
-- src:677 | Coverage B - The total liability of the Company for all damages because of all property damage sustained by one or more
-- src:678 | persons or organizations as the result of any one occurrence shall not exceed the limit of property damage liability stated in
-- src:679 | the schedule as applicable to "each occurrence".
-- src:681 | Subject to the above provision respecting "each occurrence", the total liability of the Company for all damages because of
-- src:682 | all property damage to which this coverage applies shall not exceed the limit of property damage liability stated in the
-- src:683 | schedule as "aggregate".
-- src:685 | Coverage A and B - for all purpose of determining the limit of the Company's liability, all bodily injury and property damage
-- src:686 | arising out of continuous or repeated exposure to substantially the same general conditions shall be considered as arising out
-- src:687 | of one occurrence.
@ref src:673-675
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`P&CO III Coverage A — the occurrence falls under the bodily injury aggregate` claim MEANS
    "all bodily injury to which this coverage applies" ... TRUE

@ref src:681-683
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`P&CO III Coverage B — the occurrence falls under the property damage aggregate` claim MEANS
    "all property damage to which this coverage applies" ... TRUE

§§ `IV. POLICY TERRITORY`

-- src:690 | IV. POLICY TERRITORY
-- src:692 | This insurance applies only to bodily injury or property damage which occurs within the policy territory.
@ref src:692
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`P&CO IV — the harm occurs within the policy territory` claim MEANS
    `the harm occurs within the policy territory` claim
